Committed so that `watcher.spec.ts` does not have to create this directory.

On Linux the watcher adds an inotify watch per directory, and a *second
level* directory created after the extension host started never became
watched at all -- so a file written into it fired nothing, however many
times the spec rewrote it. Two attempts at the test's own timing (a
settle, then a delete-and-rewrite retry) each passed once and failed the
run after.

The directories exist before the host starts now, so only the file is
new. That is also what a real workspace looks like: nobody creates
`db/migrate/` and a migration in it in the same millisecond and expects
the event on the next tick. `024.120`.
